1
00:05:56,470 --> 00:06:02,470
A comedy about the young at heart.

2
00:11:52,941 --> 00:11:58,941
Queen Bees is a romance, comedy, drama film directed by Michael Lembeck.

3
00:17:49,411 --> 00:17:55,411
Helen is an independent widow who moves into the Pine Grove Senior Community and
discovers it’s just like high school – full of cliques and flirtatious suitors.

4
00:23:45,882 --> 00:23:51,882
What she initially avoids leads her to exactly what she has been missing:
new friendships and a chance at love again with newcomer Dan.

5
00:29:42,352 --> 00:29:48,352
Helen Wilson, played by Ellen Burstyn.

6
00:35:38,823 --> 00:35:44,823
Dan, played by James Caan.

7
00:41:35,294 --> 00:41:41,294
Margot Clark, played by Ann-Margret.

8
00:47:31,764 --> 00:47:37,764
Jane Poindexter, played by Jane Curtin.

9
00:53:28,235 --> 00:53:34,235
Arthur Lane, played by Christopher Lloyd.

10
00:59:24,705 --> 00:59:30,705
Sally, played by Loretta Devine.

11
01:05:21,176 --> 01:05:27,176
Queen Bees is a 2021 American romantic comedy film directed by Michael Lembeck.

12
01:11:17,647 --> 01:11:23,647
It features an ensemble cast, including Ellen Burstyn, James Caan (in his final film released during his
lifetime), Ann-Margret, Christopher Lloyd, Jane Curtin, Loretta Devine, and Elizabeth Mitchell.

13
01:17:14,117 --> 01:17:20,117
It was released on June 11, 2021, by Gravitas Ventures,
and received mixed reviews from critics.

14
01:23:10,588 --> 01:23:16,588
Screenwriter Donald Martin was nominated for a 2022
Humanitas Prize for his screenplay.

15
01:29:07,058 --> 01:29:13,058
The film explores themes of control freak, forgetful
fire, repairing family connections.

16
01:35:03,529 --> 01:35:09,529
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
